===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsɪ.kəˌtɹɪks/|/sɪˈkeɪ.tɹɪks/}}
* {{hyphenation|en|ci|ca|trix}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|+|cicatrices}}

# A [[scar]] that remains after the [[development]] of new [[tissue]] over a [[recovering]] [[wound]] or [[sore]] {{qualifier|also used figuratively}}.
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1853|author=John C. Cobden|title=The White Slaves of England|publisher=Derby|location=Cincinnati|page=33|passage=Here the boy was made to strip, and the commissioner, Mr Symonds, found a large cicatrix likely to have been occasioned by such an instrument...}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1938|author=[[w:Xavier Herbert|Xavier Herbert]]|title=[[w:Capricornia (novel)|Capricornia]]|chapter=II|page=21
|passage=He stopped to stare at two old men who sat beside the fire, naked and daubed with red and white ochre and adorned about arms and legs and breasts with elaborate systems of '''cicatrix'''.}}

